.TH echo "" "Command"
.SH NAME
echo \- print arguments
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBecho [\-n] [\fIargument ...\fB]\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.HS
echo -- print arguments
Usage:	echo [ -n ] [ argument ... ]
Option:	-n	Do not print terminal newline
Copies all command arguments to the standard output.
.HE
.B echo
prints each
.I argument
on the standard output, separating consecutive arguments with a
single space, and follows the last one with a newline.
.IP \fB\-n\fR 0.4i
Suppress the trailing newline.
Recognized only as the very first argument; if it is present and
spelled exactly
.BR \-n ,
it is taken as this option and is not itself printed.
There is consequently no way to make this
.B echo
print a first argument that is literally the two characters
.BR \-n .
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.B echo
always exits with status 0.
.SH NOTES
This
.B echo
does not interpret backslash escape sequences such as
.B \e\en
or
.B \e\et
in its arguments; each argument is copied through exactly as given on
the command line.
